NAME
====

**wattle-deps** - manage the dependencies of a project

SYNOPSIS
========

**wattle deps** _verb_

DESCRIPTION
===========

**wattle deps** copies dependencies into the project in the current
directory. The sources to copy are declared under ``:vendored`` in the
project's info file. Nothing is installed under ``*prefix*``. See
`wattle-dependencies(7)` for vendoring and remote libraries.

A build made without the OS library does not include ***deps***. Each verb
reports this limitation and exits with status 1. **d** is a synonym for
***deps***.

VERBS
=====

- ***vendor***:
  Copies the sources declared in ``:vendored`` into the project. Each
  declaration is a map containing ``:name`` and ``:url``. The URL specifies
  a source as for ***install*** in `wattle-apps(1)`.

  Optional keys select what to copy and where to place it. ``:ref`` selects
  a Git branch or tag. ``:prefix`` specifies the destination directory and
  defaults to the current directory. ``:paths`` is a vector of source paths
  or pairs of source and destination paths. Without ``:paths``, the whole
  source is copied. See `<VENDORING>` in `wattle-dependencies(7)` for the
  declaration keys and an example.

  Existing files are replaced. Paths cannot be absolute or contain ``..``.
  Every declaration is checked before any source is fetched, and names must
  be unique. Vendoring records no source revision; the copied files become
  part of the project.

EXAMPLES
========

Copy the vendored sources that ``info.edn`` lists into the current directory:

````
$ wattle deps vendor
````

SEE ALSO
========

`wattle(1)`, `wattle-apps(1)`, `wattle-dependencies(7)`, `wattle-projects(7)`
